From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:11:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: apple,pmgr-s2r: add apple,apcie

The T8132 sequence takes ANS's APCIe block down at the commit and brings
it back on the wake, from the PCIe host's windows and the boot loader's
tables for them. Name that host with a phandle.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-s2r.yaml         | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-s2r.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-s2r.yaml
index 6284f3c341..f42684cd03 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-s2r.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-s2r.yaml
@@ -100,6 +100,14 @@ properties:
       goes to sleep, so that a suspend-to-RAM that never resumes ends in a
       reset. Its registers stay owned by the watchdog's own node.
 
+  apple,apcie:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      T8132 - the PCIe host whose block ANS's link shares. Its axi2af,
+      cio3pll, clkgen, phy-block, phy-ip and rc windows and the boot loader's
+      apple,tunable-* tables for them let the sequence take the block down at
+      the commit and bring it back on the wake.
+
   apple,pinctrl:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description:
